<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Info.plist — Embroidery Designer for iOS
  Copyright (C) 2026 The Catrobat Team. Licensed under AGPL-3.0.

  GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE stays YES, so Xcode merges the generated keys into
  this file at build time and nothing here needs to duplicate them. The file
  exists (US-303) because UTExportedTypeDeclarations is an array of
  dictionaries with no INFOPLIST_KEY_* build-setting form. Editing this XML is
  a normal file change, not a project-file change, so it needs no Xcode
  session — confirmed by US-308, which is also why InfoPlist.xcstrings beside
  it works with no project edit.

  US-308 (ADR-026) adds the exported `.dst` declaration below. Four things
  about it are decisions rather than boilerplate:

  - **Exported, not imported.** Apple's guidance says to declare an *exported*
    type when your app is "the canonical source of information for that type",
    and an *imported* type for "a proprietary file format the system doesn't
    declare". Tajima DST is really the latter — but the imported path also
    says to reuse the originator's identifier, and no declared DST identifier
    exists anywhere: neither Catroid nor Catty declares a `.dst` type at all,
    and the simulator resolves `.dst` to a dynamic `dyn.ah62d4rv4ge80k65y`
    placeholder (measured). The practical difference is Launch Services
    ranking, which ADR-011 does not want, so exported stands with the
    reasoning written down rather than the tension silently resolved.

  - **UTTypeConformsTo lists public.data AND public.content.** `public.data`
    is what lets Finder and the Files app represent a stored item at all;
    `public.content` is what Apple documents as the conformance that allows
    sharing over AirDrop — and this story exists to share the file, so
    omitting it would break the headline use case on the most likely
    destination. (Catty's `.catrobat` entry, the only prior art available, is
    an *imported* declaration listing public.data/public.archive with no
    public.content — a structural template only.)

  - **No LSHandlerRank.** ADR-011: we open nothing, so we claim nothing.

  - **UTTypeDescription is a localisation key**, resolved from
    InfoPlist.xcstrings. `UTTypeDeclarationTests` asserts it does not fall
    back to the key, which is the same `≠ key` check AppStringsTests makes.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>UTExportedTypeDeclarations</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>UTTypeIdentifier</key>
			<string>org.catrobat.embroiderydesigner.dst</string>
			<key>UTTypeDescription</key>
			<string>uttype.dst.description</string>
			<key>UTTypeConformsTo</key>
			<array>
				<string>public.data</string>
				<string>public.content</string>
			</array>
			<key>UTTypeTagSpecification</key>
			<dict>
				<key>public.filename-extension</key>
				<array>
					<string>dst</string>
					<string>DST</string>
				</array>
			</dict>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
